{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE scxml [\n  <!ENTITY secret SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\">\n]>\n<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"copy\">&secret;</data>\n  </datamodel>\n  <final id=\"a\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/xml006-external-entity.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/xml006-external-entity.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":29,"endLine":7,"startColumn":21,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"external entities are never read by this parser (XML 1.0 §4.4.3 lets a non-validating processor not include them)\n\n**Note:** the parser processes the internal DTD subset as XML 1.0 §5.1 requires of a non-validating processor; it never reads an external entity (XML 1.0 §4.4.3 lets a non-validating processor not include one, and reading it could disclose files or reach the network), and after a reference to a parameter entity that is not read it does not process later entity and attribute-list declarations (§5.1)\n\n**Help:** write the text in place, or declare an internal entity (`<!ENTITY name \"text\">`) in the internal subset\n\n**Spec:** XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition) §4.4 XML Processor Treatment of Entities and References","text":"external entities are never read by this parser (XML 1.0 §4.4.3 lets a non-validating processor not include them)"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":229,"start":221},"category":"syntax"},"ruleId":"XML006"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the parser processes the internal DTD subset as XML 1.0 §5.1 requires of a non-validating processor (general and parameter entities, attribute-list defaults) but never reads an external entity: §4.4.3 lets a non-validating processor not include one, and reading it could disclose local files or reach the network; after a reference to a parameter entity that is not read, later entity and attribute-list declarations are not processed (§5.1), so an entity only they would declare is not read either"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: write the text in place, or declare an internal entity (`<!ENTITY name \"text\">`) in the internal subset.\n\nSpecification: XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition) §4.4 XML Processor Treatment of Entities and References\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain XML006` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#entproc","id":"XML006","name":"XML006","properties":{"category":"syntax"},"shortDescription":{"text":"the document relies on an entity the parser does not read"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}